{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Compliance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Compliance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feedback compliance feedback compliance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Compliance.md","fileName":"Feedback Compliance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feedback Compliance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human-Computer Interaction Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Feedback","Latency","Cybersickness","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Compliance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Compliance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feedback compliance feedback compliance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Compliance.md","fileName":"Feedback Compliance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feedback Compliance","heading":"Feedback Compliance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Feedback compliance is the spatial and temporal agreement among the forms of [[Feedback]] a user receives.\n\nDirectional compliance means a virtual object moves in the same direction as the physical control. Nulling compliance means returning a device to its initial pose also returns the controlled object to its corresponding pose. Temporal compliance means feedback arrives without a disruptive delay; [[Latency]] is a common violation.\n\nWhen visual information conflicts with proprioceptive, kinesthetic, vestibular, or other cues, performance can degrade. Strong conflicts can also produce disorientation and [[Cybersickness]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Feedback","Latency","Cybersickness","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":